# Central Command local patch (no upstream number): the entity dedupe step is also
# offered existing entities by NAME, not only the vector top 15.
#
# Seam: graphiti_core/utils/maintenance/node_operations.py _collect_candidate_nodes,
# the one place resolve_extracted_nodes gets its candidates. Upstream embeds the bare
# extracted name and takes the 15 nearest stored vectors. Since the third patch a
# stored vector is name + summary, so a short name sits far from an entity with a
# long summary: on a 300-entity graph "Rivers" ranked the operator's own node
# ("Jane Rivers Doe", an 1,800-character summary) 19th, it was never a
# candidate, and five separate "Rivers" entities were created in three days (2026-11).
#
# The added lane reads the names of the group's entities that contain a word of the
# extracted name, keeps those where one name's words all appear in the other, and
# offers the closest NAME_DEDUP_CANDIDATE_LIMIT ahead of the vector hits. It decides
# nothing: the exact-name rule and the dedupe prompt downstream still do. It embeds
# nothing and writes nothing.
#
# Goes when upstream's candidate search no longer depends on the stored vector being
# the bare name, or when the third patch goes.
#
# Written for graphiti-core 0.30.2 (see PINNED_VERSION in
# central_command/integrations/graphiti_patches.py).
--- a/graphiti_core/utils/maintenance/node_operations.py
+++ b/graphiti_core/utils/maintenance/node_operations.py
@@ -63,6 +63,8 @@
